<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gorani language</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gorani is a Northwestern Iranian language spoken in parts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros</a> on both sides of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>–<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> border, closely related to Zazaki. From the 16th to the 19th century it served as the literary language of the Ardalan court at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanandaj">Sanandaj</a> and of many Kurdish poets, before Sorani largely replaced it. It is also the sacred language of the Yarsani faith.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gorani-language.jpg" alt="Gorani language" width="320" height="287" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gorani.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
